  "response_text": "The __io_putchar function is required in embedded systems because the printf function does not know by default where to send the output. It usually expects an output stream, which does not exist in microcontrollers. Implement this function helps us define how and where each character from printf should be sent (e.g. UART). This allows printf to be used in embedded systems by routing output to hardware-specific interfaces. Without __io_putchar there would be no output from printf, since there\u2019s no default output in most embedded environments.\\n",
